  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'RIDE THE PENDULUM

    One to eight competitors take turns. Three attempts
    each; total zone points win. Tied leaders receive an extra attempt, repeating
    only while tied. Solo retains a local personal best.


    PUMP: time fore/aft
    movement with the swing. Weight transfer and bounded torque feed a real hinged
    seat; pushing against its movement wastes energy. Energy is capped. Build for
    up to35s, then ACTION releases; waiting to the limit releases wherever you are.
    The truck inherits the ACTUAL seat velocity at its centre of mass, with no added
    launch impulse or calculated target.


    FLIGHT: left/right nudges the path.
    Release fore/aft once after launch to arm small range correction. The shared1.6s
    correction budget adds only bounded horizontal acceleration; no hovering or extra
    lift. After first contact, no control.


    FIRST GROUND CONTACT IS FINAL

    The
    truck centre of mass in world X/Z at its first ground contact locks10/25/50/100
    or zero. Coloured inlaid targets have closed outer boundaries; a smaller higher-value
    precision zone takes precedence where boundaries overlap. The100 bullseye is
    nearer than the50 zone. Rolling afterward cannot change points. A missed flight
    or genuine simulation timeout scores zero.


    Recorded actual-motion replays
    have three angles, slow/normal/fast, rewind and skip. They have no collision
    or scoring authority. AI-only matches advance automatically. Pause, reconnect
    and rematch retain the same ownership and setup. Offline only.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: be1034cebd9fa3643a48d11ef76e4708, type: 2}
